  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe central idea is to use a population-based optimization method combined with adaptive local search to overcome the limitations of the previous gradient-based approach. This method addresses three key challenges: (1) escaping local optima by exploring diverse regions, (2) efficiently handling the non-convex and high-dimensional search space, and (3) balancing computation time within the budget. The solution leverages stochastic sampling on a continuous domain with an exponential time decay schedule, dynamically adjusting the population size based on progress. This notationally conmines to the problem while allowing for parallel exploration patterns.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Variables: h = [0,1] \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n_points} with ||h||_1 = 49 (for n_points=98)\n- Objective: C_5 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx (discretized via np.correlate)\n- Constraints: (i) h_i \\in [0,1] \u2200i (ii) \\sum_i h_i = 49\n\nThe optimization is performed in two modes:\n- Feasible space exploration using exponential sampling: h_i \u223c truncated Laplace(0,0.5,1)\n- Local refinement using SLSQP on repaired sub-samples\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n- Initialization: Start with population_size=min(20, n_points/5) randomly sampled vectors of norm 49\n- Core evolution loop:\n  1. Steady-state replacement (\u03bc/\u03c1,(1+))\n  2. Mutant generation via covariance-adaptive jumps\n  3. Feasibility repair using:\n     \u2022 Clip extreme values to [0,1]\n     \u2022 Iterative scaling to match sum=49\n  4. Objective scoring: compute_max_overlap(h)\n- Schedule: Population size adapt \u03c3 = exp(-number_diversity_moves)\n- Repair: Iteratively clip and scale to [0,1] while tracking cumulative error\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Hyperparameter defaults: \u03c3\u2080=0.2, mutation_factor=0.8\n- Constraints: Fixed domain [0,1] and sum=49\n- Cold starts: Use L2 projection from provided initial_h_values\n\n5. Budget and robustness\n- Eval cost: O(n_points^2) per candidate\n- Deadline checks: Post each repair\n- Fallback: Reproject using softmax if variance < 1e-4\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Post-harvest validation: /np.sum(h-49)/49 < 1e-5\n- Final confirmation: compute_c5(best_h)\n- Termination: Target <0.38 | time expired\n- Output format: (h_values, bounded_C5, n_points)",
